data: {"type":"response.function_call_arguments.done","sequence_number":546,"item_id":"fc_0c21933eebe074e0016adb1d9e7f608191848141a114799462","output_index":1,"arguments":"{\"obstacle_json\":\"{\\\"status\\\":\\\"SUSPECTED_GAP\\\",\\\"location\\\":\\\"proof-draft.json, proof.lower_bound, especially the passage from the arbitrary product cover to the integrated scale-content inequality\\\",\\\"explanation\\\":\\\"I cannot responsibly submit a complete NL0 graph for this route without resolving its key content-level step. The draft asserts the pointwise Hausdorff-content lower bound after enlarging each projected last-coordinate set B_i to an interval J_i, and then takes an integral and a vanishing-error limit. Although the intended idea is plausible, the proof needs a fully quantified treatment of arbitrary cover sets, zero-diameter members, and the simultaneous scale/error limits. In particular, the claimed content inequality and the conclusion that no arbitrarily fine product covers can have bounded cost must be established directly from the precise Hausdorff-content definition, not inferred from the citation to the dimension threshold. I have not established that this implication is false, so this is an unresolved suspected gap, not a finding that the exercise is false. No new proof route was attempted.\\\",\\\"basis\\\":\\\"The supplied candidate itself lists this lower-bound content/integration argument and its zero-diameter/error treatment as unresolved (proof-draft.json, unresolved_points). I inspected the pinned HausdorffDimension source and obtained checked signatures/evidence for hausdorffMeasure_of_lt_dimH (M001) and LipschitzWith.dimH_image_le (M002); these establish only relevant dimension-theorem interfaces, not the asserted content-level inequality. No complete NL0 v2 spec/graph or structural submission was produced, and no audit PASS is claimed.\\\",\\\"partial_progress\\\":\\\"Frozen target preserved: n is a nonnegative integer, E is nonempty compact in Euclidean R^n, I=[0,1], and E×I has the concatenated Euclidean metric; conclusion dim_H(E×I)=dim_H(E)+1. No added hypotheses or theorem-valued definitions. The supplied upper-cover strategy and the D=0 projection strategy were reviewed; they appear to follow the intended route subject to their ordinary details. Pinned M evidence obtained: hausdorffMeasure_of_lt_dimH, signature as returned by probe_library in Mathlib.Topology.MetricSpace.HausdorffDimension, source Mathlib/Topology/MetricSpace/HausdorffDimension.lean, SHA256 fdc61e7f179044cd714058f209b100e51b6f8af69aff295e3ee629ed45dcee31; and LipschitzWith.dimH_image_le with the same source/hash. No source records were registered in a graph and no artifact was submitted.\\\"}\"}"}

event: response.output_item.done
data: {"type":"response.output_item.done","sequence_number":547,"output_index":1,"item":{"type":"function_call","id":"fc_0c21933eebe074e0016adb1d9e7f608191848141a114799462","call_id":"call_0e83e432769d4b57ba3fe7afdbf59a62","name":"report_obstacle","arguments":"{\"obstacle_json\":\"{\\\"status\\\":\\\"SUSPECTED_GAP\\\",\\\"location\\\":\\\"proof-draft.json, proof.lower_bound, especially the passage from the arbitrary product cover to the integrated scale-content inequality\\\",\\\"explanation\\\":\\\"I cannot responsibly submit a complete NL0 graph for this route without resolving its key content-level step. The draft asserts the pointwise Hausdorff-content lower bound after enlarging each projected last-coordinate set B_i to an interval J_i, and then takes an integral and a vanishing-error limit. Although the intended idea is plausible, the proof needs a fully quantified treatment of arbitrary cover sets, zero-diameter members, and the simultaneous scale/error limits. In particular, the claimed content inequality and the conclusion that no arbitrarily fine product covers can have bounded cost must be established directly from the precise Hausdorff-content definition, not inferred from the citation to the dimension threshold. I have not established that this implication is false, so this is an unresolved suspected gap, not a finding that the exercise is false. No new proof route was attempted.\\\",\\\"basis\\\":\\\"The supplied candidate itself lists this lower-bound content/integration argument and its zero-diameter/error treatment as unresolved (proof-draft.json, unresolved_points). I inspected the pinned HausdorffDimension source and obtained checked signatures/evidence for hausdorffMeasure_of_lt_dimH (M001) and LipschitzWith.dimH_image_le (M002); these establish only relevant dimension-theorem interfaces, not the asserted content-level inequality. No complete NL0 v2 spec/graph or structural submission was produced, and no audit PASS is claimed.\\\",\\\"partial_progress\\\":\\\"Frozen target preserved: n is a nonnegative integer, E is nonempty compact in Euclidean R^n, I=[0,1], and E×I has the concatenated Euclidean metric; conclusion dim_H(E×I)=dim_H(E)+1. No added hypotheses or theorem-valued definitions. The supplied upper-cover strategy and the D=0 projection strategy were reviewed; they appear to follow the intended route subject to their ordinary details. Pinned M evidence obtained: hausdorffMeasure_of_lt_dimH, signature as returned by probe_library in Mathlib.Topology.MetricSpace.HausdorffDimension, source Mathlib/Topology/MetricSpace/HausdorffDimension.lean, SHA256 fdc61e7f179044cd714058f209b100e51b6f8af69aff295e3ee629ed45dcee31; and LipschitzWith.dimH_image_le with the same source/hash. No source records were registered in a graph and no artifact was submitted.\\\"}\"}","status":"completed"}}

